Current operating circuit with five THKs with expected timeline to return to six THK operation several months away. 

The longstanding accepted mode of operation is that circuit cannot function with less than five THKs', N'Increase Recovery ', 10091, N'01 - Imagens/01 - Antes/7946.jpeg', N'LRWT Feed line restricted limiting flow of wash solution and causing a reduction in recovery. Current ly operating circuit with five THKs with expected timeline to return to six THK operation several months away. The longstanding accepted mode of operation is that circuit cannot function with less than five THKs resulting in a sustained period of incurring elevated losses. ', N'01 - Imagens/02 - Depois/7946.jpeg', N'Four THK operation was modelled and walked down in the field to determine feasibility. SCR completed to determine required logic changes and risk assess the new mode of operation. Total losses associated with four THK operation calculated to be 3.7 nickel tonnes for the duration of the cleaning. Recovery gain for three months on five THK operation with restricted LRWT Feed line calculated to be 40 nickel tonnes. Net gain calculated at 36.3 Ni tonnes', NULL, N'Yes the problem was solved. The model correctly predicted the metal loading to recovery circuits during the four THK operating period', N'Challenge the Status Quo', 750, 3, N'otmização do 5S, padronização e ganhos com saúda da equipe que faz esse manuseio ', '2026-01-30T00:00:00.000', '2026-02-04T15:46:18.000', 1010774, NULL, 1);
